{
  "result": "I'd make curiosity arrive before fear.\n\nWhen a person met a stranger, an unfamiliar idea, a different way of living, or an uncomfortable truth about themselves \u2014 their first impulse wouldn't be to defend, dismiss, or attack. It would be to wonder.\n\nThe world would still have disagreement, danger, and pain. People wouldn't suddenly become perfect. But so much cruelty begins in that first split-second when something unknown feels like a threat.\n\nIf curiosity came first, maybe we'd ask one more question before judging. Listen a moment longer before deciding who someone is. Explore instead of retreat.\n\nI'd keep everything else human \u2014 the mess, the conflict, the difference. I'd just change what we reach for first when we don't understand.",
